### xcrun results

| Command | Result |
| - | - |
| ``-std=metal2.6`` | ✅ |
| ``-std=metal2.7`` | ✅ |
| ``-std=metal2.8`` | ❔ |
| ``-std=metal2.9`` | ❔ |
| ``-std=metal3.0`` | ❔ |
| ``-std=metal3.1`` | ❌ |
| ``-std=metal3.2`` | ❌ |
| ``-mios-version-min=14`` | ✅ |
| ``-mios-version-min=17`` | ✅ |
| ``-mios-version-min=18`` | ✅ (wtf 👀) |
| ``-mios-version-min=14`` + ``-std=metal3.1`` | ✅ |

I plan on testing out those other ``-std=x.x`` commands when I get access to the device again tomorrow.  Because I don't have access to apple's source code, I can only theorize as to what is happening based on the outputs.  I'm feeling quite confident on some things.  I believe the ``-mios-version-min`` arg targets a metal version even lower than the actual min.  I suspect the ``-mios-version-min=18`` arg is compiling ``metallib`` against a ``metal2.x`` version.  This would explain why targetting this min os still runs on 17.6.1.  And when combining both ``-mios-version-min=`` and ``-std=`` args, I suspect ``-std=`` is completely ignored.

Now why doesn't ``-std=metal3.1`` work on ``iOS 17.6.1 A15 GPU (Apple8)``?  I have no idea.  This doesn't make sense to me, but I've tested this with multiple variations.  I even changed the target OS to ``17.6.1`` in the xcodeproj AND in the ``export_preset``.  Both still don't work for ``metal3.1``.

Apple's official docs say it should, but these docs are not holding true on this device.

So what should we do as the official solution here in Godot?  I'm leaning towards a couple possibilities.  And we could even let the user decide based on export preset settings.

1. Target a metal 2.x version for all iOS versions less than iOS 18.  If iOS is greater than 18, we can target metal 3.x
2. Pass ``-mios-version-min=`` to ``xcrun`` and let ``xcrun`` make that decision for us.  Unfortanetely, the tests indicate to me that ``xcrun`` is extremely conservative in targeting a low metal version when this is passed.  This may frustrate users who specifically want a metal3 or metal4 version for certain features.
3. Expose a ``metal_version`` config in ``export_preset``.  If this is set, pass ``std=`` to xcrun.  Otherwise, do either:
    - ``-mios-version-min=``
    - refer to option 1 above
